  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Primary path & result",
      "items": [
        "Question \u00e2\u2020\u2019 FastAPI \u00e2\u2020\u2019 session job \u00e2\u2020\u2019 coordinator \u00e2\u2020\u2019 model clients.",
        "Search, evidence validation and report synthesis run within bounded research stages.",
        "Job events and the final report return to the browser over SSE; the return is omitted to keep one readable path. [server/api/research.py:269\u00e2\u20ac\u201c292]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authentication is conditional",
      "items": [
        "Cloud mode verifies the bearer against Supabase /auth/v1/user, then checks job and record ownership.",
        "Browser Google sign-in uses PKCE; anonymous users have owned guest workspaces and a five-run research allowance.",
        "With Supabase entirely unconfigured, research and assistant routes retain local unauthenticated mode. [server/main.py:42\u00e2\u20ac\u201c74; server/workspace.py:78\u00e2\u20ac\u201c94]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Persistence & isolation",
      "items": [
        "Research checkpoints and final state are written by the server job worker, not by the pure research coordinator.",
        "Supabase records use RLS; server requests use backend-only privileged credentials with explicit owner filters.",
        "PDF reads follow current workspace record ownership; browser IndexedDB retains local history/drafts. [server/api/research.py:139\u00e2\u20ac\u201c152,241\u00e2\u20ac\u201c251; server/workspace.py:62\u00e2\u20ac\u201c76; supabase/migrations/20261010200448_pdf_transfer_read_ownership.sql:1\u00e2\u20ac\u201c4]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Assistant & uploaded PDFs",
      "items": [
        "Hybrid chat retrieves only its active context, sends bounded history and streams Gemini answers with validated citation IDs.",
        "PDF uploads are capped at 25 MiB; pypdf runs in a disposable subprocess with a 90-second timeout. Extraction becomes page-level chat context.",
        "Collection chat can combine owned reports, conversations and PDFs. This is keyword RAG, not a vector database. [server/api/research.py:354\u00e2\u20ac\u201c439; app/pdf_documents.py:8\u00e2\u20ac\u201c19,56\u00e2\u20ac\u201c64; server/productivity.py:69\u00e2\u20ac\u201c139]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "External inputs & model routing",
      "items": [
        "Tavily discovers URLs; the fetcher rejects private addresses, pins DNS, rechecks redirects and limits content. Retrieved content is untrusted evidence.",
        "Gemini handles planning, synthesis, conflict analysis and chat. Groq handles extraction, source quality and review tasks.",
        "Model output is parsed into schemas and checked against evidence; it is not executed. [tools/webpage.py:14\u00e2\u20ac\u201c62; app/llm/routing.py:25\u00e2\u20ac\u201c45; app/llm/router.py:65\u00e2\u20ac\u201c94; app/evidence.py:13\u00e2\u20ac\u201c42]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Secondary capabilities & limits",
      "items": [
        "Collections, section feedback, expiring report-share links, source-review checkpoints and opt-in alerts reuse the same API and owned persistence.",
        "Alerts run in the backend's lifespan worker, not an external scheduler. Public share reads are capability-based exceptions to authenticated routes.",
        "Jobs and replay buffers are process-local: no Redis, distributed queue or dedicated worker service is shown. Actual deployed instances and ingress limits are not verified. [server/main.py:20\u00e2\u20ac\u201c32; server/productivity.py:142\u00e2\u20ac\u201c273; server/api/research.py:53\u00e2\u20ac\u201c69]"
      ]
    }
  ]
}